# Line endings: the repository is authored with LF. Windows checkouts with
# core.autocrlf=true would otherwise rewrite these files to CRLF.
#
# js/data/astrologie.js is generated by scripts/generate-astrologie-data.cjs and
# is compared byte for byte against a fresh generation in tests/astrologie.mjs.
# Any end-of-line conversion would make that test fail on a Windows checkout
# while passing on Linux CI, so the file must be stored and checked out verbatim.
js/data/astrologie.js -text

# Das V1-Manifest wird in tests/tarot-decks-v2.cjs bytegenau geprüft; eine
# CRLF-Konvertierung beim Windows-Checkout würde den Hash verändern.
assets/tarot/nachtatelier-v1/manifest.json -text

# js/data/farbwelten.js is generated from content/farbwelten/*.md by
# scripts/generate-farbwelten-data.cjs; store it verbatim so regeneration stays
# idempotent on Windows checkouts.
js/data/farbwelten.js -text

# js/data/articles-markdown.js is generated from data/articles/*.md by
# scripts/generate-articles-data.cjs and compared byte for byte in --check.
# Store and check it out verbatim so a Windows autocrlf checkout cannot break
# the comparison while Linux CI stays green.
js/data/articles-markdown.js -text

# Der Medien-Katalog wird bytegenau gegen die Erzeugung geprueft
# (scripts/migration-baseline/build-media-catalog.cjs --check). Eine
# CRLF-Konvertierung beim Windows-Checkout wuerde den Vergleich brechen.
docs/migration-baseline/media-catalog.csv text eol=lf
